WEBVTT

00:01.060 --> 00:04.060
Wheat Flour

01:06.920 --> 01:07.420
From: Kanae
I'm throwing it out!

02:48.020 --> 02:50.390
I Want My Money

02:48.020 --> 02:50.390
Notice

02:50.390 --> 02:52.770
Foreclosure

02:56.690 --> 02:59.530
01  "Beethes and Motes and Otowakan"

02:59.530 --> 03:00.650
Warning

03:04.400 --> 03:05.450
I'm home.

03:06.030 --> 03:07.870
Welcome home, Kanae.

03:09.850 --> 03:11.120
My.

03:15.130 --> 03:17.960
Don't throw it out, Kanae!

03:18.300 --> 03:20.450
Why? How could you just throw out my stuff?

03:20.450 --> 03:21.940
I've been telling you since last month.

03:21.940 --> 03:23.500
You wouldn't come pick it up.

03:23.500 --> 03:25.220
Has it been that long?

03:25.520 --> 03:27.220
To be exact,

03:27.450 --> 03:30.350
you received an email 42 days ago.

03:30.720 --> 03:32.200
Right, Pad-kun?

03:32.200 --> 03:34.560
I was, like, busy and stuff.

03:34.960 --> 03:37.420
But remember? You said I could leave it there

03:37.420 --> 03:39.690
since you weren't using it.

03:39.690 --> 03:41.950
I told you, I'm moving.

03:41.950 --> 03:43.580
Oh, you're serious?

03:43.580 --> 03:45.800
We already have a buyer.

03:45.800 --> 03:46.240
But...

03:46.240 --> 03:48.150
Welcome home, Kanae!

03:48.150 --> 03:48.960
Who...

03:48.960 --> 03:50.630
Look!

03:56.150 --> 03:57.640
What are you doing?

03:57.640 --> 03:58.250
Are you hurt?

03:58.250 --> 03:59.890
I'm totally fine.

03:59.890 --> 04:01.110
You have a nosebleed.

04:01.110 --> 04:02.260
On purpose.

04:03.750 --> 04:06.480
No roller shoes in the house.

04:06.480 --> 04:09.830
Perhaps it's in forbidden acts
that the truth is hidden.

04:12.530 --> 04:13.550
Your boyfriend?!

04:13.550 --> 04:14.760
You have a boyfriend now?!

04:14.760 --> 04:15.690
No way.

04:15.690 --> 04:16.740
Is that it?

04:16.740 --> 04:18.540
Is that why you're throwing out my stuff?

04:18.540 --> 04:19.670
I told you, "no."

04:19.670 --> 04:20.990
So who's he, then?

04:22.630 --> 04:25.400
Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.

04:25.720 --> 04:27.490
Pleased to meet you.

04:28.060 --> 04:30.260
Amadeus Mozart?

04:30.260 --> 04:30.770
Yup.

04:31.070 --> 04:32.000
You can call me Motes.

04:32.000 --> 04:33.750
I'm Sousuke.

04:33.750 --> 04:34.460
Nice to meet you.

04:34.850 --> 04:36.430
Hey, your boyfriend's pretty cool.

04:36.430 --> 04:37.730
I told you, he's—

04:41.880 --> 04:42.900
A fire?!

04:48.080 --> 04:50.890
Wh-What the hell are you doing?

04:51.810 --> 04:53.100
Making gyoza.

04:54.140 --> 04:55.270
Tasty Gyoza

04:54.360 --> 04:57.400
I'm making gyoza!

04:57.640 --> 04:58.520
What?!

04:58.520 --> 05:00.620
Why do you need all this to make gyoza?

05:00.620 --> 05:02.690
Cooking is all about fire.

05:03.190 --> 05:04.820
That's what it said in this book.

05:05.050 --> 05:06.860
No, that's not the point.

05:07.400 --> 05:09.320
Didn't I tell you not to

05:09.320 --> 05:12.040
come in this room?

05:12.280 --> 05:14.960
Gyoza are splendid, are they not, girl?

05:14.960 --> 05:16.740
Listen to me.

05:15.770 --> 05:18.670
The punch of their flavor is like a timpani!

05:19.020 --> 05:22.330
Meat and oil: a delicate, vibrant ensemble,

05:19.920 --> 05:21.510
Uh, so—

05:22.330 --> 05:24.030
like the sound of a violin.

05:24.030 --> 05:24.980
Chives and cabbage!

05:24.030 --> 05:24.980
Hey.

05:24.980 --> 05:28.390
And one cannot forget the garlic!

05:28.960 --> 05:32.870
And like the sound of an oboe, it
is all caressed gently by the skin!

05:32.870 --> 05:34.180
Carbohydrates!

05:34.180 --> 05:35.790
Source of power!

05:35.790 --> 05:37.640
Not only is it nutritionally complete,

05:37.640 --> 05:40.440
in its gestalt, it resounds in harmony!

05:40.650 --> 05:43.890
How magnificent gyoza is!

05:44.260 --> 05:51.680
Like a powerful orchestral hit, its juices flow with every bite, blowing me away every time.

05:45.510 --> 05:47.160
Hey, is he your boyfriend, too?

05:47.160 --> 05:49.750
Please don't make things even worse.

05:49.750 --> 05:52.410
His name is Ludwig van Beethoven.

05:51.680 --> 05:54.040
Fascinating. Utterly fascinating.

05:52.670 --> 05:54.120
You can call him Beethes.

05:54.530 --> 05:56.330
He might freak out if you don't
call him Beethes-<i>san</i>, though.

05:56.520 --> 05:58.420
Just who could say this is complete?

05:56.730 --> 05:58.420
Beethes-san, huh?

05:58.820 --> 06:00.700
Yes... It is perfect darkness,

06:00.700 --> 06:03.670
blacker than black.

06:03.890 --> 06:06.560
You're just going to scorch
the gyoza with this thing.

06:06.560 --> 06:07.630
Indeed!

06:07.630 --> 06:08.670
In that very instant!

06:08.670 --> 06:10.850
A glimmer, like a staccato!

06:10.850 --> 06:12.780
It is the soul of the matter!

06:12.780 --> 06:14.160
Put it away, please.

06:14.160 --> 06:18.020
It prevents the aroma from
escaping, locking in the flavor.

06:18.370 --> 06:21.510
By frying it instantly with
overwhelming firepower...

06:21.510 --> 06:22.900
Put it away.

06:23.150 --> 06:25.400
It begins: my revolutionary gyoza!

06:25.400 --> 06:27.400
I won't stop telling you: put it away.

06:27.400 --> 06:28.490
Feuer!

06:48.870 --> 06:49.870
Firepower.

06:50.180 --> 06:52.390
Perhaps that was a little
too much firepower.

06:53.750 --> 06:54.630
Girl,

06:55.520 --> 06:56.530
want it?

06:58.350 --> 06:59.420
I do not.

07:02.540 --> 07:05.020
Hey, Kanae, what's up with those guys?

07:05.340 --> 07:07.500
Dad's acquaintances, apparently.

07:07.500 --> 07:09.300
Your dad's back, huh?

07:09.300 --> 07:10.530
He's not.

07:10.790 --> 07:14.040
They came here with invitation
letters, and now they won't leave.

07:14.040 --> 07:15.710
I see.

07:15.710 --> 07:18.400
Your dad sure does bring
in all kinds of things.

07:18.400 --> 07:21.340
Dogs, cats, shoebills...

07:21.670 --> 07:23.640
He's so selfish.

07:23.640 --> 07:25.420
He never stops making trouble for me.

07:25.420 --> 07:27.720
Come on, if you're going to
have those guys living here,

07:27.720 --> 07:29.590
can't you keep my stuff here, too?

07:28.830 --> 07:29.840
Nope.

07:29.840 --> 07:33.140
I never said they could
live here to begin with.

07:33.140 --> 07:35.660
I can't even fit it all in my house, though,

07:35.660 --> 07:37.630
even if you tell me to clean up.

07:37.630 --> 07:40.020
There's the guitar and the turntable, and...

07:40.330 --> 07:42.010
Why don't you throw it out?
You aren't using it.

07:42.010 --> 07:42.720
Dude!

07:42.720 --> 07:45.060
An instrument is a musician's soul.

07:45.060 --> 07:46.320
Who's a musician?

07:46.320 --> 07:47.180
Me.

07:47.180 --> 07:49.080
You can't even play a single instrument.

07:49.550 --> 07:53.300
Talent takes time to flourish.

07:53.300 --> 07:55.950
It takes me a while to get warmed up.

07:55.950 --> 07:57.510
I'm a slow starter, you know?

07:57.510 --> 07:58.990
You're just trying to get girls, aren't you?

07:58.990 --> 07:59.910
Yup!

08:00.130 --> 08:02.330
You never change, do you, Sousuke?

08:02.330 --> 08:03.950
These days,

08:03.950 --> 08:07.210
I'm hooked on desktop
music stuff. Isn't that cool?

08:07.210 --> 08:09.920
DTM. Do you underst—

08:11.120 --> 08:13.780
Just clean it up, or I'm throwing it out.

08:14.490 --> 08:16.250
Owie!

08:41.850 --> 08:43.120
It's so tasty.

08:43.740 --> 08:45.670
Oh, you.

08:54.340 --> 08:57.010
My, how did you get so dirty?

08:57.330 --> 08:57.920
Don't you—

08:57.920 --> 08:59.080
Bleh!

09:09.980 --> 09:11.430
Otowa here.

09:12.720 --> 09:13.390
What?

09:14.180 --> 09:15.350
Demolish?

09:15.350 --> 09:16.110
Tomorrow?

09:16.390 --> 09:17.120
Yes.

09:17.420 --> 09:19.920
I just got a call from a contractor.

09:20.220 --> 09:23.000
It's just been decided that
it's getting torn down.

09:23.000 --> 09:26.500
So please pack your stuff and
leave by the end of today.

09:26.500 --> 09:30.160
Where am I to go to perfect my gyoza?

09:30.160 --> 09:31.380
I don't care.

09:31.630 --> 09:35.240
Go fry gyoza by the river or behind
a Chinese restaurant or something.

09:35.240 --> 09:38.710
It is illegal to start fires
outdoors without a permit.

09:39.890 --> 09:42.010
What grief!

09:42.010 --> 09:44.640
Is this fate knocking, as well?

09:44.920 --> 09:48.160
Fate always forces a separation.

09:48.460 --> 09:50.550
You, too, Sousuke. Got it?

09:50.550 --> 09:52.560
Are you really tearing it down?

09:52.560 --> 09:54.580
I thought this was your
grandma's precious mansion.

09:55.110 --> 09:55.890
Yeah.

09:56.200 --> 09:57.170
Everything?

09:57.170 --> 09:58.070
Everything.

09:58.070 --> 09:59.290
All of it?

09:59.290 --> 10:00.330
All of it.

10:00.630 --> 10:02.210
You're turning it into an empty lot?

10:02.210 --> 10:02.790
Yes.

10:03.170 --> 10:04.280
What about Hasshie-kun?

10:04.280 --> 10:06.120
We already know who's adopting him.

10:06.380 --> 10:07.520
My room, too?

10:07.520 --> 10:09.280
It isn't your room.

10:09.790 --> 10:10.840
What about that?

10:12.460 --> 10:14.310
It doesn't even work, anyway.

10:14.680 --> 10:16.440
It's all going away?

10:17.790 --> 10:20.390
It's already been decided.

10:21.250 --> 10:24.600
Hey, then is there any reason
those two need to clean up?

10:31.030 --> 10:35.030
Everyone leave!

10:38.740 --> 10:41.320
Man, I pissed her off.

10:42.010 --> 10:43.780
What are you two going to do?

10:43.780 --> 10:45.450
Do you have a place to go?

10:46.900 --> 10:49.460
What? No way, my place won't work.

10:52.210 --> 10:54.620
I should have done this sooner.

11:09.520 --> 11:10.890
A ball?

11:11.240 --> 11:12.100
Yes.

11:12.400 --> 11:13.900
We all danced together.

11:14.220 --> 11:16.070
To the music.

11:18.040 --> 11:19.530
It looks so fun.

11:25.010 --> 11:28.290
This mechanical organ used to work properly.

11:29.000 --> 11:31.370
It played all kinds of music.

11:32.120 --> 11:33.930
That was a long time ago.

11:34.420 --> 11:36.480
Let's hold a ball!

11:36.480 --> 11:38.930
Hm? Kanae.

11:39.510 --> 11:43.220
It plays music when you
turn this thing, right?

11:43.540 --> 11:45.850
If there's music,

11:45.850 --> 11:49.850
we can have a ball, right?

11:50.760 --> 11:52.000
Kanae.

11:52.000 --> 11:53.600
Ow, ow.

11:53.600 --> 11:54.520
Oh, dear.

11:54.960 --> 11:56.020
I'm okay.

11:56.020 --> 11:57.740
This doesn't hurt.

11:57.740 --> 11:58.890
One more—

11:58.000 --> 11:59.100
Stop it.

11:59.100 --> 12:01.360
All right, all right.

12:01.980 --> 12:05.480
Then when I get even bigger,

12:05.480 --> 12:08.020
I'll hold a ball for you.

12:10.220 --> 12:12.830
Thank you, Kanae.

12:13.110 --> 12:15.840
You're a strong, kind child.

12:17.190 --> 12:20.030
I'll be looking forward to the ball.

12:20.030 --> 12:20.880
Yup.

12:32.350 --> 12:35.270
Kanae's family is from some

12:35.270 --> 12:38.190
distinguished noble lineage or something.

12:38.910 --> 12:42.400
They were still wealthy
while her grandma was alive,

12:42.400 --> 12:44.970
but her dad was pretty eccentric.

12:45.200 --> 12:48.450
I heard he was doing research of some kind.

12:48.880 --> 12:51.540
He abandoned home and went wandering

12:51.770 --> 12:53.730
all over the place, using
up his inheritance.

12:54.290 --> 12:58.070
So his wife got sick of him and left.

12:58.370 --> 13:01.670
She's always had it rough.

13:02.840 --> 13:04.380
You sure know a lot.

13:04.380 --> 13:07.180
We've known each other since we were little.

13:07.180 --> 13:08.550
But Sousuke,

13:08.890 --> 13:11.930
how are we going to deal with this
mountain of junk by tomorrow?

13:11.930 --> 13:13.640
Mountain of <i>treasures</i>!

13:13.640 --> 13:16.310
And how am I supposed to

13:16.310 --> 13:18.190
take it home on such short notice?

13:20.630 --> 13:22.460
I feel something coming.

13:22.460 --> 13:23.420
Are you serious?

13:23.420 --> 13:24.960
Do it in the bathroom!

13:24.960 --> 13:25.800
No.

13:25.800 --> 13:27.910
I feel like I'm about to remember something.

13:27.910 --> 13:29.080
Remember what?

13:31.020 --> 13:31.910
No good.

13:32.380 --> 13:34.380
Forgetting is a basic truth
of the human condition.

13:34.380 --> 13:36.830
Yet such imperfection is
a source of vexation.

13:37.080 --> 13:39.770
Unpleasant. Upsetting. Upsetting indeed.

13:39.770 --> 13:42.560
Is this, too, a challenge of fate?

13:42.960 --> 13:43.920
Very well!

13:44.430 --> 13:46.760
I shall prevail!

13:47.250 --> 13:49.010
You're complicated.

13:49.660 --> 13:51.180
Kanae's a good girl.

13:51.500 --> 13:52.680
You sure?

13:52.680 --> 13:54.670
She can be scary when you make her angry.

13:54.670 --> 13:56.300
She's kind and upright.

13:56.300 --> 13:59.140
She's a classy lady with an upright bosom.

14:00.690 --> 14:02.220
I can feel it coming, and yet...

14:04.810 --> 14:05.750
I know.

14:06.100 --> 14:07.630
I'll fry some gyoza.

14:09.190 --> 14:10.790
Yeah, let's!

14:09.620 --> 14:11.090
What's the deal with you two?

14:18.670 --> 14:21.610
I never got it to work.

14:22.930 --> 14:26.270
I'm sorry, Grandmother.

14:35.050 --> 14:35.930
What the?

14:35.930 --> 14:38.300
It appears the teardown is about to begin.

14:43.970 --> 14:45.980
I apologize for the short notice.

14:46.280 --> 14:49.710
With that said, we've already
taken ownership of the building.

14:49.710 --> 14:53.200
I believe we've given you
ample time to vacate.

14:53.460 --> 14:55.910
I know. I apologize.

14:55.910 --> 14:57.310
Kanae!

14:57.310 --> 14:58.300
Sousuke.

14:58.300 --> 14:59.470
Why are you—

14:59.470 --> 15:01.130
Don't tell me the other two are here, too.

15:01.130 --> 15:02.520
I wouldn't know.

15:02.520 --> 15:04.340
Are you seriously demolishing this place?

15:05.290 --> 15:06.280
Stop it.

15:07.760 --> 15:08.810
Brilliant.

15:09.390 --> 15:11.840
The skin, the filling,
the way it's wrapped...

15:11.840 --> 15:14.140
This is perfection in every aspect!

15:14.390 --> 15:16.040
And now we reach

15:16.750 --> 15:18.520
the climax!

15:21.890 --> 15:24.060
I <i>just</i> came up with this yesterday.

15:24.530 --> 15:26.650
My own talent gives me chills.

15:37.830 --> 15:40.130
Seriously, this is raw.

15:40.130 --> 15:42.290
Are you sure you want to
go through with this?

15:42.850 --> 15:43.880
It's too late.

15:43.880 --> 15:46.750
But my stuff's still in there.

15:47.070 --> 15:49.310
It's too late.

15:59.790 --> 16:00.820
That sound...

16:02.030 --> 16:03.330
The organ.

16:08.970 --> 16:09.800
No.

16:10.330 --> 16:11.700
I can't take it.

16:11.700 --> 16:12.500
Idiot!

16:13.530 --> 16:14.450
Stop!

16:14.950 --> 16:17.090
Please stop!

16:38.870 --> 16:39.900
Please.

16:40.640 --> 16:42.010
No more.

16:42.760 --> 16:44.790
Don't destroy it!

16:55.130 --> 16:55.960
Kanae...

16:59.790 --> 17:03.320
Musik!

17:12.120 --> 17:15.670
I have been deprived of the opportunity
to consume my supreme gyoza.

17:15.960 --> 17:18.470
That it falls to the ground,
never to satisfy my tongue...

17:18.720 --> 17:19.890
Is this, too, fate?

17:20.240 --> 17:21.190
Then!

17:21.190 --> 17:24.690
I shall strangle fate itself!

17:25.000 --> 17:28.240
I shall not yield to fate!

17:28.240 --> 17:33.940
Spielen wir unsere Musik!

17:52.370 --> 17:58.350
Cower before my Musik, fate!

18:09.520 --> 18:11.210
What's this music?

18:11.590 --> 18:14.070
Symphony No. 6 in F Major,

18:14.370 --> 18:15.910
"Pastorale."

18:16.210 --> 18:19.590
The sixth symphony by German composer

18:19.590 --> 18:23.590
Ludwig van Beethoven, completed in 1808.

18:23.950 --> 18:26.960
Opus number 68.

18:43.100 --> 18:45.230
The people from the drawing.

18:45.230 --> 18:46.260
Damn.

18:46.260 --> 18:47.430
Pad-kun, record!

18:47.430 --> 18:48.270
Fine, fine.

18:51.990 --> 18:52.960
Kanae.

18:55.330 --> 18:56.440
Welcome.

18:56.790 --> 18:59.150
Grandmother?

19:04.320 --> 19:07.630
Indeed, <i>this</i> is what
I was trying to remember!

19:07.630 --> 19:09.170
Passion overwhelming!

19:09.170 --> 19:10.750
Melodies aweaving!

19:11.100 --> 19:15.100
My power, Musik!

19:17.570 --> 19:19.550
You must have been holding back, too, huh?

19:22.720 --> 19:23.550
And you guys, too.

19:47.870 --> 19:48.930
It's so fun.

19:48.930 --> 19:51.080
I can't help but dance.

19:54.320 --> 19:55.460
We did it.

19:55.760 --> 19:57.000
The ball.

19:57.250 --> 20:00.540
This was a place of happiness,

20:00.540 --> 20:02.890
filled with music and smiles.

20:04.120 --> 20:05.320
Grandmother.

20:06.250 --> 20:09.540
I'll protect this mansion.

20:09.980 --> 20:12.300
Passione!

20:13.560 --> 20:15.900
Passione!

20:16.650 --> 20:20.240
Spielen wir unsere...

20:20.240 --> 20:24.240
Spielen wir unsere...

20:24.240 --> 20:26.010
Musik

20:24.990 --> 20:28.160
Das Ende!

20:26.010 --> 20:28.920
Musik

20:36.320 --> 20:38.410
What was that?

20:38.410 --> 20:39.710
Is this mansion haunted?

20:39.710 --> 20:41.380
Sousuke. Sousuke.

20:42.710 --> 20:43.900
Grandmother.

21:02.880 --> 21:04.320
Yes, it appears so.

21:05.430 --> 21:08.950
It seems to be the ClassicaLoids.

21:10.310 --> 21:13.850
We've found the escaped ClassicaLoids,
Beethoven and Mozart.

21:13.850 --> 21:15.290
Really?

21:15.720 --> 21:17.510
Is this luck?

21:17.510 --> 21:19.340
Or is it destiny?

21:19.340 --> 21:21.960
What shall we do, Great Bach-sama?

21:23.180 --> 21:24.940
Andante.

21:37.010 --> 21:38.680
Thank you.

21:38.680 --> 21:39.600
Sure!

21:43.150 --> 21:45.900
Man, that was awesome yesterday!

21:46.230 --> 21:48.970
Beethes-san, Motes-san,
how did you even do it?

21:48.970 --> 21:49.850
I don't know.

21:49.850 --> 21:52.660
I simply gave into my overflowing emotions.

21:52.660 --> 21:54.770
We're geniuses, after all.

21:54.770 --> 21:56.830
It's not all that surprising what we did.

21:56.830 --> 21:57.890
It's only logical.

21:57.890 --> 22:00.310
Holy crap, dude! I'm floored!

22:00.310 --> 22:01.340
Let me study with you.

22:01.690 --> 22:04.380
I'll come to this mansion every day.

22:04.380 --> 22:05.500
Umm...

22:05.500 --> 22:07.840
Why are you assuming you
two are living here?

22:09.960 --> 22:11.470
I thought you decided not to move out.

22:12.010 --> 22:14.490
That's got nothing to do with this!

22:15.330 --> 22:17.400
I must redo my gyoza.

22:17.400 --> 22:20.020
You're so hot when you're angry, Kanae.

22:18.630 --> 22:20.020
Come on...

22:20.020 --> 22:21.640
Can we talk about my studying with you?

22:21.640 --> 22:23.450
I swear, I can make myself useful.

22:23.450 --> 22:24.490
Dammit,

22:24.750 --> 22:28.550
all of you, get out!

22:28.990 --> 22:31.990
To be continued

24:02.000 --> 24:26.730
02 "Make Musik!"

24:02.410 --> 24:04.400
Just what are ClassicaLoids?

24:04.400 --> 24:07.830
They appear whimsical, but
they also seem terrifying.

24:07.830 --> 24:09.800
Who are the ClassicaLoids?

24:09.800 --> 24:13.780
And what is this bizarre
phenomenon of "Musik?"

24:13.780 --> 24:16.180
Let's not jump to conclusions.

24:16.180 --> 24:18.000
This gang of misfits in this here Otowakan,

24:18.000 --> 24:20.560
this dump— rather, this classical house—

24:20.560 --> 24:23.030
does it not appear that they themselves

24:23.030 --> 24:25.110
are not aware of who they are?

24:25.830 --> 24:26.410
What's this?

24:26.410 --> 24:27.570
What is this vibe?

24:27.570 --> 24:28.960
Musik!
